    [Misc] Remove unused benchmark report converter script (#19200)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fixes #18237
    
    This PR removes two dead files:
    
    - `benchmarks/scripts/convert_json_to_markdown.py`
    - `benchmarks/scripts/perf_result_template.md` (only referenced as the
    former script's default template argument)
    
    Why they are dead code:
    
    - The current aisbench-based benchmark CI uploads raw JSON artifacts
    directly and never invokes this script.
    - Nothing in the repo references either file: no CI workflow, script,
    test, or documentation (`git grep convert_json_to_markdown` / `git grep
    perf_result_template` on `main` return nothing but the script's own
    default argument, which is deleted here).
    - `benchmarks/README.md` only points users to
    `run-performance-benchmarks.sh` and the raw JSON files under
    `benchmarks/results/`; it never mentions this converter.
    
    Confirmed with the author of #18251 that there is no remaining use case
    for this script.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: wangkunpeng <1289706727@qq.com>

